<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-09-25T20:05:25Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Germany news: Parliament approves fuel tax cut</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2df7a630c699794ca93d2045b925e81cb2052f10231bec3117769cb58fe959b2</id><updated>2026-09-25T20:04:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T19:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-parliament-approves-fuel-tax-cut/live-79424882--bd35c461e842.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-parliament-approves-fuel-tax-cut/live-79424882?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German lawmakers hope to drive down fuel prices by cutting taxes on gas and diesel from October 1. Meanwhile, Germany's defense minister visited Budapest to ramp up defense and military ties. DW has the latest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>AfD, CDU ban new Holocaust 'stumbling stones' in Heidenau</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:153e3b37150fd35aeaa7a642d751f99a65361fd242a99f21ee620a9ac3371a87</id><updated>2026-09-25T20:05:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T14:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/afd-cdu-ban-new-holocaust-stumbling-stones-in-heidenau/a-79433919--bafd061ca07a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afd-cdu-ban-new-holocaust-stumbling-stones-in-heidenau/a-79433919?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Activists, politicians and representatives of Holocaust victims reacted with anger after the center-right CDU party joined forces with the AfD to ban new Stolpersteine (stumbling stones) in the eastern town of Heidenau.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Volkswagen, Audi to recall almost 1 million cars in Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c3afe90e2bf2ce8e79d82a0a7568fcad19f79949e7303f3919cc7399a2213129</id><updated>2026-09-25T20:04:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T09:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/volkswagen-audi-to-recall-almost-1-million-cars-in-germany/a-79426960--b707dbde3045.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/volkswagen-audi-to-recall-almost-1-million-cars-in-germany/a-79426960?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Volkswagen and its subsidiary Audi are to recall nearly a million vehicles in Germany due to a potential steering fault.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Jürgen Klopp starts Germany job with shaky Netherlands draw</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a95d71cec97524ca9fb4fc795b37aeaeee8c221d569cb2d590a647ffd4482df1</id><updated>2026-09-25T20:04:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T22:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/j_rgen-klopp-starts-germany-job-with-shaky-netherlands-draw/a-79420143--fa995d928e4d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jürgen-klopp-starts-germany-job-with-shaky-netherlands-draw/a-79420143?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A late Netherlands goal denied Jürgen Klopp a win in his first match as Germany coach. The former Liverpool and Borussia Dortmund boss has big ambitions, but the game showed he's going to need more time to achieve them.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Berlin officially withdraws Olympics bid</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6daf9cf57f2dd6a5c2dea987ed8b4811308d0f04f40e147bfe6d37c30e665ad6</id><updated>2026-09-25T20:04:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T12:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-berlin-officially-withdraws-olympics-bid/live-79406294--30622a12ce08.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-berlin-officially-withdraws-olympics-bid/live-79406294?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Berlin's decision to withdraw its Olympic bid means that only Munich and the western Rhine/Ruhr region are left in the running as potential Olympic hosts. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Economic institutes double growth forecast for 2026</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bb4102068e4a23c9541dda1d4a9434b0ff00b23814bcbadf1980c1f21d9c9c41</id><updated>2026-09-25T20:04:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T08:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-economic-institutes-double-growth-forecast-for-2026/a-78168080--b4403b4ba952.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-economic-institutes-double-growth-forecast-for-2026/a-78168080?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Experts predict German GDP growth will double to 1.3% this year but warn of structural difficulties ahead. The picture is complicated, they say, especially because of uncertainty in the energy sector.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Berlin Airport briefly suspends flights over drone sighting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce01857bcad32a2284b11392f131a225ccae30c2b3f950d01053e9f41b39161d</id><updated>2026-09-25T20:04:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T19:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/berlin-airport-briefly-suspends-flights-over-drone-sighting/a-79403865--84b3e93d15cb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/berlin-airport-briefly-suspends-flights-over-drone-sighting/a-79403865?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Airspace over the German capital was closed for about 45 minutes after a drone was spotted on the runway. Flights have resumed but are experiencing delays.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bundesliga, other top European leagues call for major FIFA reforms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ffe4fd89fab3f8599c026406abfec4875d1753b020ecd19d4ca47b5ed6de40d2</id><updated>2026-09-25T20:05:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T13:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bundesliga-other-top-european-leagues-call-for-major-fifa-reforms/a-79431717--3029f0ff55b2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bundesliga-other-top-european-leagues-call-for-major-fifa-reforms/a-79431717?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Bundesliga and three other leading European football leagues have said major reforms to world-governing body FIFA are "essential." However, they stopped short of calling for the resignation of boss Gianni Infantino.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>After several difficult years, economists now expect German economy to grow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:728c576a7f12a8834514cfddf9b77cfcef6da8f4e2ffac8155b3bf5b224f1582</id><updated>2026-09-25T20:04:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T17:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/after-several-difficult-years-economists-now-expect-german-economy-to-grow/a-79418591--9a99d252976e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/after-several-difficult-years-economists-now-expect-german-economy-to-grow/a-79418591?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's economy is growing again, but recovery remains on shaky ground. High government spending is keeping the economy afloat, while energy prices, a shortage of skilled workers and debt continue to weigh on it.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Political psychology: Why extremist parties are thriving and what democratic politicians can do against it</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a8d7ebd2008dd2eacf046e56634354ff0430baee294628c3e3ff4e5f3e549405</id><updated>2026-09-25T20:04:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T14:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/political-psychology-why-extremist-parties-are-thriving-and-what-democratic-politicians-can-do-again/a-79410960--440643795892.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/political-psychology-why-extremist-parties-are-thriving-and-what-democratic-politicians-can-do-against-it/a-79410960?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Far-right and far-left parties are celebrating success after success, leaving moderate politicians in the dust and worrying many Germans. Political psychology helps us understand what's behind growing polarization.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Three-way battle for power in world chess: Who will be elected FIDE president in Samarkand?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:41465734b777a0c6b6cf12bfbbc18b0f3bd2fe4b340f6c4eab9c5fbe099e667e</id><updated>2026-09-25T20:04:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301--bc60333e85fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The era of Russian presidents is coming to an end at the World Chess Federation (FIDE). Two Germans and one Kazakh are up for election. Among the issues at play are money, Kremlin influence, and unanswered questions.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Oktoberfest 2026: Everything you need to know</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3cbccf9af32cdf63c9de6475900a5f472f85406f291fd41048d07be45ce9b4c0</id><updated>2026-09-25T20:04:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T09:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/oktoberfest-2026-everything-you-need-to-know/a-79311285--1e3ee9d16248.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/oktoberfest-2026-everything-you-need-to-know/a-79311285?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">This year, AI will be used to manage overcrowded situations. Find all the numbers surrounding the fest — including the price of water!</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry></feed>
